186575575 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we notice that the function has precisely two distinct roots, $x=-1,$ and $x=3.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=-1,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=3,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=3,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=\\frac{1}{9}(x+1)^{2}(x-3)^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575654 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "60068a08-fa3f-50ca-8965-30a471415f04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575654 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575659 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575659 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "673d9b83-3ff3-5843-9dcb-506dafb7b36d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575659 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186326706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575671 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575671 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "93468536-e912-5d59-af9e-1d96c93b2485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575671 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186326705 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
